  <div class="lp__note">
    <strong>Notes for decision:</strong><br/>
    • The new mark is dark (#191919) organic paths on transparent — it needs the warm cream radial background to read clearly.<br/>
    • The "PI" text in the logo uses Gautreaux-Light (Adobe font, not loaded on site) — it will render in the system fallback serif at current sizes, though it's largely invisible below 80px anyway.<br/>
    • At sm (22px) the mark detail is lost — consider keeping the italic "PI" text fallback at ≤24px rather than swapping to the full mark.<br/>
    • The standalone (no-circle) treatment in Surface 5 may be the right move for larger contexts (drawer header, AskPICTA) while the circle avatar is kept for message bylines where size is fixed.
